TSFUTL is run from the command line with two command-line arguments.
That is

              TSFUTL  input output <Enter>

where <Enter> denotes pressing the key of that name.
The first command-line argument, input, can be any file name of
a file that contains the input commands for TSFUTL.  The second
command-line argument is the file name for the file that will
contain what TSFUTL produces as it processes the commands in  the
input file.  The file names can have paths attached so long as
the name with path is less than 64 characters. 

Here is an example:

   TSFUTL  TSFUTL.IN   TSFUTL.0  <Enter>

See the file named INPUT for the descriptions of the commands and
examples of how they are used.  As an example of commands in 
TSFUTL run the input example.  The DTSF file is in the same 
directory so execute the following on the command line:


TSFUTL INPUT OUT

Make sure that you have plenty of space on the disk.  This command
will create about 10 more MB of files!



